  "definition": "In this source, sigma refers to sigma receptors, a type of cell membrane receptor that can bind several psychoactive substances, including some opioids, and affect changes inside cells. Unlike the main opioid receptor classes, their natural endogenous ligands are not known from the information provided here.",
